@startuml
' claim: what an ABI change needs is decided by comparing abi/layout.txt with the last release, line by line
start
:headers under app/include/<root> -> gcc -g -aux-info -> DWARF + declarations;
:generated layout program (or abi/layout.c) + sections + #define constants + unnamed enums;
:abi/layout.txt as the gate writes it now;
if (differs from the committed file?) then (yes)
  :refused: say which raise, then --update;
  stop
endif
:compare with the file at the newest reachable tag v<x.y.z> (else the previous commit),\nthen every commit that changed it, each with its own VERSION;
if (an existing line changed or removed,\nor a member added to an existing struct) then (yes)
  :needs a raised MAJOR;
elseif (new names in covered categories,\nor a *_ABI_MINOR constant that only rose) then (yes)
  :needs a raised MINOR;
elseif (only new categories) then (yes)
  :tooling change: nothing to raise;
else (identical)
endif
:--exports: the .so exports exactly the declared functions as name@@NODE_major;
stop
@enduml
